these are the death certificates of four  palestinian boys killed during the war  in gaza last summer  samir manama is a lawyer who works with  the palestinian human rights  organization  he's been gathering evidence of possible  war crimes  we're questioning people taking  photographs looking at medical reports  recording the names of all the victims  we're collecting all the evidence we can  each sheet in these boxes corresponds to  one human fate  few of these cases have been examined by  judges  if they have it's been in an israeli  military court  human rights activists see the  international criminal court as the only  chance to hold israeli commanders and  politicians accountable  it's the time to reconsider the issue of  accountability as long as we are talking  about war crimes it's not palestine  israel it's the victims the victims are  far than ever from achieving their  rights where to go  this is the only place  the bakker family hopes the icc agrees  to hear their case  it's tough for them to go back to the  beach where their ten-year-old son and  three of his cousins were killed last  summer  another son al-muntasir was injured and  remains traumatized  when i come here where the children were  killed  it's almost as if it just happened  i can barely look at the scene  it used to be a special place for me  since i'm a fishermen  the boys were playing here on july 16th  2014 when they were caught in an  explosion almond sir is still too  disturbed to talk about it  this is the immediate aftermath  eyewitnesses including foreign  journalists reported two explosions in  quick succession  they were believed to be shells fired by  the israeli navy who say they did fire  on hamas targets at the time  an israeli military court is currently  examining the case  but the bakar family and palestinian  human rights activists see the  international criminal court in the  hague as a better guarantee of justice  even if the case could take years
 

